PART 2 -- COVARIANT reading (timelike phidot_c present): what B(X) actually couples
==================================================================================================
  [ok ]  4. *** dX at LINEAR order = 2 Phi phidot_c^2  -- set by the METRIC potential, NOT by dphi ***
         dX_linear = 2*Phi*phidot_c**2  (the local scalar gradient enters X only at O(eps^2))
  [ok ]  5. Phi~ (covariant) = Phi*(A0 + A' phidot^2 - B' phidot^4)/(A0 - B0 phidot^2)  -- carries B'
         Phi~ = Phi*(A0 + Ap*phidot_c**2 - Bp*phidot_c**4)/(A0 - B0*phidot_c**2)
  [ok ]  6. *** Psi~ (covariant) carries NO B' at all: disformal is invisible to the spatial sector ***
         Psi~ = Psi - Ap*Phi*phidot_c**2/A0;  d(Psi~)/dB' = 0
  [ok ]  7. *** Phi~,Psi~ are proportional to Phi (metric), independent of dphi -> the coupling is a CONSTANT G-rescaling, NOT a MOND fifth force ***
         shift-symmetric A(X),B(X) + timelike bg => G_eff=const*G, no RAR shape at linear order
  [ok ]  8. *** the sole linear-order dphi coupling is g~_0i = B0 phidot_c d_i dphi (a PREFERRED-FRAME off-diagonal term) -- not dynamics, not lensing ***
         g~_0i (linear) = B0*gi*phidot_c
  [ * ] COVARIANT VERDICT:
         the shift-symmetric disformal coupling with a timelike cosmological background produces
         (a) a constant G-rescaling in the diagonal sector (no MOND), and (b) a preferred-frame g~_0i.
         To get a genuine dphi-sourced MOND force one must break shift symmetry (A(phi), = RAQUAL) -> Part-1 under-lensing,
         OR adopt the local reading (Part 3).  Either way the disformal B is chained to a preferred-frame term.

