PART 5 -- VERDICT
==================================================================================================
  [ * ] DELIVERABLE 1 (lensing gate):
         the disformal B CANNOT give MOND-dynamics + factor-2 lensing + gamma_PPN=1 as a clean package.
         - Covariant reading (Part 2): shift-symmetric A(X),B(X) + timelike bg => constant G-rescaling, NO MOND;
           the only linear dphi coupling is a preferred-frame g~_0i. To get MOND you must break shift symmetry
           (RAQUAL) and then light is conformally blind => UNDER-LENSES (Part 1).
         - Local reading (Part 3): isotropic lensing IS repairable (honest, matches sf27), but ONLY with a nonzero
           disformal amplitude, which is an unavoidable ANISOTROPIC STRESS (strong gamma_PPN=1 fails) and needs B ~ (c^2/a0)^2.
  [ * ] DELIVERABLE 2 (preferred-frame gate):
         the SAME disformal coupling, with the timelike background restored, sources a static preferred-
         frame g~_0i = B0 phidot_c d dphi, an alpha_1 carrier ~ B' phidot_c^4 (w U), and an alpha_2 carrier in g~_00
         ~ phidot_c^2 (A' + phidot^2 B') (w^2 U) -- all NONZERO, scaling as phidot_c^2*coupling (the known Bekenstein-
         Sanders/aether result), NOT protected by any symmetry, set by FIXED cosmological couplings (low-acceleration =>
         B large, not kernel-suppressed).  The closed alpha_2 coefficient needs the full coupled O(w^2) solve (not done,
         stated honestly); but it is nonzero and removable ONLY by phidot_c -> 0, which deletes the disformal mechanism.
  [ * ] OVERALL:
         *** DEAD -- the pure disformal scalar hits the SAME lensing-vs-preferred-frame pincer as AeST/TeVeS. ***
         The factor-2 lensing a vector supplies (a SPATIAL preferred direction entering g~_ij at LINEAR order) cannot
         come from B(X) d phi d phi: the scalar's spatial gradient enters g~_ij only at O(eps^2) and only as anisotropic
         stress, while its coupling to the timelike background is exactly what generates an unsuppressed alpha_2.
         This is precisely why TeVeS needed a vector; the disformal scalar does not evade the no-go.

